			]
			shape: "rsquare"
			tasks: [{
				entity: "mowziesmobs:ferrous_wroughtnaut"
				icon: "mowziesmobs:wroughtnaut_spawn_egg"
				id: "5E2C35CCBEA640AA"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			title: "&#B0B0B0&lL&#ACACAC&li&#A8A8A8&lv&#A4A4A4&li&#A0A0A0&ln&#9C9C9C&lg &#949494&lA&#909090&lr&#8C8C8C&lm&#888888&lo&#848484&lr&#808080&l, &#787878&lt&#747474&lh&#707070&le &#696969&lF&#656565&le&#616161&lr&#5D5D5D&lr&#595959&lo&#555555&lu&#515151&ls &#494949&lW&#454545&lr&#414141&lo&#3D3D3D&lu&#393939&lg&#353535&lh&#313131&lt&#2D2D2D&ln&#292929&la&#252525&lu&#212121&lt"
			x: -1.5d
			y: 9.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["206E6EE1994EA27F"]
			description: [
				"\"Long ago, a cult of creatures started worshipping the sun's energy, believing in its primordial power that can destroy anything when forsaken. Umuvthi stands as their last guardian, a feathered tyrant lying still beneath the acacia trees, its feathers the color of dying light. It sleeps and relaxes, while its masked cultists kneel. They believe the sun will answer them. They do not know they are the sacrifice. When Umuvthi rises, its followers throw themselves between you and their god. Their wounds become its healing. Strike the bird, and a masked believer falls silent. And when it tires of patience, it smites its foe with the sole energy it believes in. The cult believes they seek a supreme being beyond the sun. They do not know the Virtue has never once looked their way. But Umuvthi knows. That is why it keeps them praying. When the bird falls, its feathers dim. The masks shatter, and something far above finally turns its head...\""
				""
				"Threat Level: ☠☠"
				"Summon: Find an Umvuthana Grove in arid biomes."
				"Recommended Armor: Titan"
			]
			id: "549ABEB50C4B50DF"
